# Crafting_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Recipe-based creation systems (survival_crafting).

## 2. This document owns
- Recipe registry: inputs, stations, time, yields, failure rules.
- Crafting progression: what unlocks recipes (discovery/leveling).
- Batch/quality rules and material substitution policy.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- Material definitions and economy — Resource_And_Economy.
- Station/building placement — Base_Building_Design.
- Item results — Item_Design (linked).

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Crafting philosophy / 2. Recipe registry / 3. Stations / 4. Discovery & unlocks / 5. Time & batch / 6. Quality & failure / 7. Substitution policy / 8. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Crafting vs Resource: transformation rules here; material values there.
- A recipe references materials and outputs by ID; it never restates stats.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Every recipe's inputs/outputs resolve to registered materials/items.
- Substitution policy is total (every material: substitutable or not).
